# Draft knowledge entry: Boost.Python test_package runtime libpython on HarmonyOS PC
id: DRAFT-boost-python312-test-runtime-libpython
trigger_tool: conan|cmake|test_package|ssh
phase: testing|runtime
error_signature: "libpython3.12.so.1.0.*cannot open shared object file|undefined symbol: Py_|Boost.Python.*runtime|boost_python312.*Py_"

severity: 2
category: boost|python|runtime|test-package|ohos
match_keywords: Boost.Python, test_package, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, conanrun, libpython3.12.so.1.0, binary-sign-tool, Py_Initialize, HarmonyOS PC

title: Boost.Python test_package must expose the OHOS CPython libdir at runtime
root_cause: >
  Conan VirtualRunEnv adds packaged libraries to the runtime environment, but the OHOS CPython
  shared library may live outside the Conan package graph under the device Python prefix. A
  Boost.Python consumer can link successfully and still fail at execution because the dynamic
  loader cannot find libpython3.12.so.1.0 or resolve Python C API symbols.
affected_scope: >
  OHOS test_package or shadow CI runs for Boost.Python and downstream C++ bindings that link
  libboost_python312.so against an external CPython runtime.
verification_cmd: |
  conan create archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1 -pr:h ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -r=ohpcd --build=missing
  # The runtime test should print the consumer success line without missing libpython or Py_* loader errors.

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: prepend-cpython-libdir-while-preserving-conanrun
rec_description: >
  Keep VirtualRunEnv enabled for Conan package libraries, sign the OHOS executable before running
  it, discover the selected CPython library directory, and prepend that directory to LD_LIBRARY_PATH
  only for the runtime invocation.
rec_command: |
  VirtualRunEnv(self).generate()
  python_libdir = os.path.dirname(self._discover_python()["library"])
  command = 'LD_LIBRARY_PATH="{}:${{LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}}" "{}"'.format(python_libdir, executable)
  self.run(command, env="conanrun", cwd=self.build_folder)
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-test-package-runtime-env

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: diagnose-loader-before-relaxing-test
fallback_description: >
  If the test still fails, inspect the executable and packaged Boost.Python library with readelf or
  loader logs to identify the exact missing SONAME. Do not replace the runtime test with a compile-only
  check unless the platform cannot execute target binaries and that limitation is explicitly recorded.
fallback_command: |
  rg -n "libpython3.12|cannot open shared object file|undefined symbol: Py_" build logs
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: runtime-loader-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: "self.run.*ignore|LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.*without.*conanrun|test_package.*compile only"
forbid_1_reason: The problem appears only when the dynamic loader resolves Boost.Python and CPython together.
forbid_1_consequence: The package can look green while downstream Python bindings fail on device startup.
forbid_2_pattern: "copy.*libpython.*package_folder|bundle.*system Python"
forbid_2_reason: The CPython runtime belongs to the target Python installation; vendoring it into Boost hides ownership and update boundaries.
forbid_2_consequence: Downstream packages may run against a stale or duplicate Python runtime.

principles: real-runtime-validation, preserve-conanrun, runtime-owner-boundary
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

